    "summary": "The configurator won't put five drawers in one hex base. A full base takes no drawers. A quarter base takes none either. A half base takes exactly one, on its cut face. I built the closest version it accepts: one north-half base (piece:0,0,0;half-n) with one drawer (drawer:0#0,0#cut). The build check reports no rule errors, and the collision check came back clear. I didn't run the usual finishing steps (end caps on the open faces and bolting the joints) because you asked for nothing else to be added. Three side faces are left open. Getting five drawers would take more bases, for example five half bases, and you ruled that out.",
